text:
Jules Park: Quick follow-up from the UI review: compaction across modals, toasts, and inline action buttons is inconsistent in the dashboard. We need a small set of tokens and a clear behavior matrix.
Sam Carter: Noted. I saw three problems: 1) icon-only buttons look crammed in compact table rows, 2) toasts overlap floating controls, 3) compact modals clip focus rings.
Mei Wong: For tokens, proposal: `--compact-gap`, `--compact-icon-size`, `--overlay-offset`, and `--focus-offset-compact`. Keep defaults separate from compact overrides.
Arjun Desai: Agree. Suggested values: `--compact-gap: 6px`, `--compact-icon-size: 16px`, `--overlay-offset: 12px`, `--focus-offset-compact: 4px`. Those kept UI tight but still accessible.
Jules Park: If we reduce visual icon to 16px we must preserve tap targets. Add `--icon-hit-area: 44px` and document the pattern: visual size vs hit area.
Sam Carter: Will do. Also, toasts should anchor under any pinned toolbar by default. Otherwise they obscure controls. We need `--toast-anchor-top` token and a rule that respects pinned headers.
Mei Wong: Proposal: token `--toast-anchor-top: calc(var(--pinned-toolbar-height) + var(--overlay-offset))`. That makes it composable.
Arjun Desai: Behavior question: when a modal opens, should toasts remain visible above modals for critical alerts? I'd prefer default toasts go under modals, critical get `data-toast-priority="high"` and a higher z-index.
Jules Park: Yes. Default under modals. Add accessible exception: critical toasts must include clear CTA and be keyboard-focusable.
Sam Carter: Found a visual bug: compact modal with `--focus-offset-compact: 4px` still clips the ring on iOS Safari. Might need to increase to 6px or add outline-offset fallback.
Mei Wong: Let's set `--focus-offset-compact: 6px` for now. We can add a platform-specific note.
Arjun Desai: Small copy suggestion: replace terse toasts like "Saved" with slightly helpful ones: "Settings saved  changes applied" (or localized variant). Product okayed this earlier.
Jules Park: Good. Add i18n key `toast.saved.settings=Settings saved  changes applied`. Also remind teams to include context in quick toasts.
Sam Carter: Accessibility-bot ran a quick passive check: icon-only buttons in table rows missing `aria-label` on two stories. Will add lint rule to prevent merging.
accessibility-bot: Automated check: 2 icon-only button instances missing aria-label. See /storybook/button-variants and /dashboard/compact-row.
Mei Wong: Implementation snippets I'll land in the tokens file: 
```
:root {
  --compact-gap: 6px;
  --compact-icon-size: 16px;
  --icon-hit-area: 44px;
  --overlay-offset: 12px;
  --toast-anchor-top: calc(var(--pinned-toolbar-height) + var(--overlay-offset));
  --focus-offset-compact: 6px;
}
```
Arjun Desai: CSS helpers: 
```
.icon { width: var(--compact-icon-size); height: var(--compact-icon-size); }
.icon__hit { padding: calc((var(--icon-hit-area) - var(--compact-icon-size)) / 2); }
.toast { top: var(--toast-anchor-top); }
.surface--modal .toast:not([data-toast-priority="high"]) { z-index: 0; }
.toast[data-toast-priority="high"] { z-index: 9999; }
```
Sam Carter: QA notes: add visual tests for narrow viewports where toolbar is sticky + toast appears. Also add a11y regression test for focus ring clipping on modal open.
Mei Wong: Docs: I'll add a matrix showing when to use compact tokens vs default, how to preserve hit targets, and examples of promoted toasts.
Jules Park: Action items: Mei add tokens + docs, Sam add lint rule + visual tests, Arjun add behavior for toast priority and ensure keyboard handling, accessibility-bot will re-run checks after PR. Target next minor.
design-bot: Draft created: design/tokens/compact-spacing.yml (preview).
Arjun Desai: One more micro-ux thought: when a toast with action appears and a modal is open, instead of promoting toast above modal, prefer moving the toast to a persistent inline area in the modal header to keep context. Less surprising.
Jules Park: Love that. Add design pattern: `if (modalOpen && toast.hasAction) -> mount toast in modal header slot` with code sample in docs.
Sam Carter: Great. I'll prototype the modal-slot approach and include fallback for older browsers.
Jules Park: Thanks all. If we land this today, we can include the tokens in the patch and update component docs. :rocket:
